# Milestone: M5
# Covers: at (cond) body — rising-edge fire; body runs once when cond
#         transitions false→true; does not re-fire on same-direction writes.
#
# The condition is re-evaluated whenever a slot it reads is written, and
# the body runs on a strand the emitting line's pump drains, so the
# counter is settled by the time the next line reads it.
#
# The trigger() indirection is not required any more -- a bare top-level
# `x = 10` reaches the same drain -- but it is kept because it is what the
# fixture has always driven, and one less thing changing at a time.

var x = 0;
var fired = 0;
at (x > 5) fired = fired + 1;
var trigger = function() { x = 10 }; trigger();
fired
[00000000] 0
[00000000] 0
[00000000] nil
[00000000] 10
[00000000] 1
